# Line endings are LF on every system, whatever git's local setting says.
#
# Measured on 2026-09-29, first run of Crusetra Routing's Windows matrix: Git for Windows checks
# text files out with CRLF by default, and the README check then read a README whose
# multi-line figure blocks no longer matched what the generator produces (the single-line
# blocks matched, which is the signature). Nothing in the repository had changed; the checkout
# had. This repository carries the same figures module (src/figures.ts) and also compares bytes
# elsewhere: the sealed record and its signature are hashed as written.
#
# `text=auto` lets git tell text from binary; `eol=lf` fixes the working-tree ending. The
# index already holds every text file as LF (see `git ls-files --eol`), so this file changes
# no committed byte; it stops a checkout from changing them. src/gitattributes.test.ts holds
# the line below in place.
* text=auto eol=lf
